            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0166" n="1000" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1000"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1445a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-01T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1727. For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1328. For your confidential information. Supplementing Department’s 1648,
                    September 27, 3 p.m., our 1282. Swedish sailing vessels will be permitted to
                    traverse the danger zone <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> to Sweden
                    provided (1) that if any such vessel carry any quantity of petroleum or its
                    by-products or foodstuffs as cargo, such petroleum and its by-products and
                    foodstuffs must be so stowed in the hold of the vessel beneath cargo of a
                    different nature as to make it manifestly difficult for any submarine to remove
                    such petroleum or its by-products or foodstuffs, and provided (2) that no such
                    vessel will be permitted to sail with any quantity of brass, copper, or other
                    similar metals as such. Repeat to Owen as confidential information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
